**Use the minimal D436 wording, then run a controlled outside test before the authorized gate rerun.** The outside set is thin for the exact failure class, so its result must be called a diagnostic.

- **Wording:** omit the case-matching examples. Add only the two proposed D436 sentences, subject to the whole-request audit. Keeping the frozen wording does **not** remove the existing ambiguity about listing an outcome already decided by an answer; it avoids A2’s additional wording changes. [Audit](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/astra-a2/audit-2.md>)
- **Outside cases:** `week-10-06:c1/clean-2` is the closest total-plus-part case; frozen Astra declined it once in three draws. `week-10-06:c1/clean-6` is an event-plus-consequence case, declined three times, but is not a figure. `week-10-06:c1/clean-3` is unsuitable as a clean target: HBM and DRAM may need an undefined combined measure. I found no established outside target for the shortage-plus-growth shape, so **there are not enough confirmed close matches to prove the full class**. [Stored cases](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-reference-control-2026-11-16/cases.json>), [Astra screens](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/astra/RESULT.md>)
- **Pass rule:** require the fresh frozen arm to exercise the target failure; otherwise **inconclusive**. Require at least two fewer failed sends in the edited arm, accepted replacements under both agreed and strict counts, all justified-decline controls retained, and no new hard-line or material defect by topic. Read both arms blind, including the previously observed over-listing harm. A stopped draw or missed planted control is not measured. Price the chosen population and retries before sending; three draws of both arms may exceed the $1 estimate.
- **Gate rerun:** Alex authorized it, but the 44 have now informed the proposed change. It is therefore a **reused, exposed acceptance set**, not an independent generalization test. Keep the six lines and both unresolved-point countings unchanged, report that limitation and the unresolved due-day ruling, and use fresh material later to assess generalization. The outside diagnostic must pass its prewritten rule first. [D649](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:1>)

CONSENSUS: test the example-free D436 wording outside the 44 with exercised controls and a fixed comparative rule; rerun the authorized gate only if that diagnostic passes.
